WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.851 --> 00:00:05.774
On line 3 in hall B too-light cartons keep coming out of the filling unit.

2
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.955
You are the engineer.

3
00:00:08.673 --> 00:00:12.156
After the shift you stay with the team lead to fix it for good.

4
00:00:13.253 --> 00:00:14.704
That takes four things.

5
00:00:15.461 --> 00:00:20.419
Find the cause, read the process, know the cost and make the line more reliable.

6
00:00:21.447 --> 00:00:25.255
That makes four stations, from problem solving to reliability.

7
00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:29.587
The first station is Engineering problem solving.

8
00:00:30.288 --> 00:00:33.028
You look for the root cause of the too-light cartons.

9
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.095
First you go and look where it happens.

10
00:00:36.795 --> 00:00:38.827
Only then do you look for a cause.

11
00:00:39.859 --> 00:00:42.936
You stand in an Ohno circle and draw a why tree.

12
00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:47.649
Without this you treat the symptom, and the problem can come back.

13
00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:52.655
The second station is Measurement and SPC in depth.

14
00:00:53.351 --> 00:00:56.231
You follow the fill weight with data, not by feel.

15
00:00:57.244 --> 00:01:00.193
After a changeover you weigh one carton first.

16
00:01:01.009 --> 00:01:04.353
Then you weigh equal batches and count the too-light ones.

17
00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:09.199
You do a first-off check and plot that count on an np chart.

18
00:01:10.281 --> 00:01:14.379
Without this you can react to routine noise or miss a real change.

19
00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.185
The third station is Cost engineering.

20
00:01:18.875 --> 00:01:21.093
You want to know what the problem costs.

21
00:01:22.128 --> 00:01:25.228
A too-light carton goes in the bin and costs money.

22
00:01:25.926 --> 00:01:28.980
An improvement costs money too, so you work it out.

23
00:01:30.047 --> 00:01:33.762
You add up the cost of poor quality and work out the cash saving.

24
00:01:34.762 --> 00:01:38.303
Without this nobody knows whether the fix is worth the effort.

25
00:01:39.658 --> 00:01:43.187
The fourth station is Reliability and asset strategy.

26
00:01:43.881 --> 00:01:46.714
You make the line more reliable, where it counts.

27
00:01:47.778 --> 00:01:49.682
Not every part counts the same.

28
00:01:50.405 --> 00:01:52.576
You look at what happens when it fails.

29
00:01:53.602 --> 00:01:57.828
You put the parts in a risk matrix and make an FMECA.

30
00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.782
Without this you do not know which part to tackle first.

31
00:02:03.161 --> 00:02:04.322
This is the whole map.

32
00:02:05.055 --> 00:02:08.712
The four stations of Making the plant better lie in one zone.

33
00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.865
First Engineering problem solving,

34
00:02:11.993 --> 00:02:15.488
from finding the root cause to kaizen and the value stream.

35
00:02:16.491 --> 00:02:18.941
Then Measurement and SPC in depth,

36
00:02:19.103 --> 00:02:22.307
from measurement systems to SPC on the shop floor.

37
00:02:23.421 --> 00:02:27.797
Then Cost engineering, from cost price and hour rates to savings.

38
00:02:28.793 --> 00:02:34.099
Finally Reliability and asset strategy, from failure to decisions based on data.

39
00:02:35.153 --> 00:02:36.500
That is how they connect.

40
00:02:37.226 --> 00:02:42.103
First you find the cause, and measurements show whether the process really changes.

41
00:02:43.119 --> 00:02:44.814
Cost shows what it is worth.

42
00:02:45.552 --> 00:02:47.932
Reliability says where to do it first.

43
00:02:48.984 --> 00:02:52.246
Each station is a module with four levels per topic.

44
00:02:53.043 --> 00:02:54.982
Start with what your line needs now.
